 ## Evaluating a props base with known operands (`resolver/evaluate.rs`)

-`resolve_base_as_chain` evaluates three kinds of props base when their operands are known, without a checker: a conditional whose check is a literal and whose constraint is `keyof X`, a literal or a union of literals (`RecipeProps<"button">` picks its branch); an indexed access, chained and through generic interface members and aliases (`ConfigRecipes["button"]["__type"]`); and a mapped type over `keyof X` or a literal union, one prop per key with the key variable bound. A homomorphic mapped type without `?`/`-?` keeps each source member's optionality and description. Anything else (an `infer`, an unbound generic) evaluates to `None` and keeps the warning and `composes` entry. `alias_display` uses the same evaluator for an argument that reads a member (`ConditionalValue<ButtonVariant["size"]>` prints the member's type), and so does any indexed access at the type level (`primitives::resolve_indexed_access`), before the `CSSProperties`/`HTMLAttributes` member table, which answers only when no declaration does (next section). A member read binds each ancestor's `extends` arguments to the arguments it was reached with, so `CSSProperties["width"]` through `Properties<string | number>` gets `Width<string | number>`. It also reads curated mode's React index and treats an unimported `React.X` as React's UMD global. A member read goes through an ancestor that is an alias, and through a mapped type over `keyof T` with the key bound (csstype's `Fallback<T>`); a conditional whose check is a member read is decided when that member's type is a set of string types, and a member the payload object doesn't declare takes the false branch. Type-level conditionals use the same evaluator, which decides assignability over one small set of atoms (`Atom`: literals, `string`, `number`, `boolean` as `false | true`, `null`, `undefined`) on both sides. A generic alias that is a conditional over a bare type parameter distributes over the members of the argument bound to it (`named::expand_alia